{"base_rate":0.21139430284857572,"brier":0.39410134932533736,"bss":-1.3640395221530084,"bss_hi":-0.9988516117114294,"bss_lo":-1.8227049140700633,"chart":{"base":[336.1,157.4],"fp":[140.9,114.0],"lead":"62,276.3 272,266.7 482,271.8 692,252.7","note":{"base":"skill -1.36 — higher than 0% of cities","fp":"low end -5pp, high end +59pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 86% of cities","rel":"promised 16% → rained 3%; promised 100% → rained 52%"},"rel":"162.5,452.7 389.7,409.5 540.7,406.5 636.8,371.5 689.6,242.3"},"country":"TG","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.4639880059970015,"ess":506.99422212711306,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Lome</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Lome rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 8 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>52%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(5%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 667 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 5.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -1.36, ranked 212 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(211&ndash;212) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>60</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>80%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>52%</b></td><td class='num'>141</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">8 of 9 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Lome</b> <span class=\"muted\">Togo</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">8 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-1.36</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>211&ndash;212\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>667 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Lome &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Lome\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"76.46246153846154,342.8 152.4363076923077,242.0 216.86430769230768,174.8 267.45907692307696,124.39999999999998 310.2249999