ecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"267.45907692307696\" cy=\"331.6\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 71%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 60 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"310.2249999999999\" cy=\"339.5333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 80%&amp;#10;It rained 15% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"339.88384615384615\" cy=\"326.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 25% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"368.41737704918035\" cy=\"292.4918032786885\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 94%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"392.45074626865664\" cy=\"311.3731343283582\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 52% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 141 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.66936170212773\" cy=\"193.54609929078015\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(21%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Lome the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (-1.08) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-4.02).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>168</td><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'>-4.024</td><td class='num'>39.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>176</td><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'>-1.300</td><td class='num'>50.6%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>-1.296</td><td class='num'>51.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>149</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>-1.083</td><td class='num'>42.8%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":6.12874,"lon":1.22154,"n":667,"n_cities":213,"name":"Lome","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.16,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.052153846153846155,"n":65,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.37,"lo":0.16,"mean":0.26676923076923076,"n":65,"obs":0.06153846153846154,"sig":true},{"hi":0.53,"lo":0.37,"mean":0.44876923076923075,"n":65,"obs":0.12307692307692308,"sig":true},{"hi":0.67,"lo":0.53,"mean":0.5916923076923077,"n":65,"obs":0.13846153846153847,"sig":true},{"hi":0.76,"lo":0.67,"mean":0.7124999999999998,"n":60,"obs":0.11666666666666667,"sig":true},{"hi":0.85,"lo":0.76,"mean":0.7962820512820513,"n":78,"obs":0.15384615384615385,"sig":true},{"hi":0.92,"lo":0.85,"mean":0.8768852459016394,"n":61,"obs":0.2459016393442623,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.92,"mean":0.9447761194029849,"n":67,"obs":0.1940298507